        "topic": "Accounting Equation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2007",
        "question_text": "<p>If the assets of a business are $20,000 and the liabilities are $8,000, what is the owner's equity?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The accounting equation is: <b>Assets = Liabilities + Owner's Equity</b>. Rearranged, <b>Owner's Equity = Assets - Liabilities</b>. Thus, $20,000 - $8,000 = $12,000.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
